1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,030
Thank you for calling the Tourist Line.

2
00:00:03,030 --> 00:00:06,250
There are many different ways of getting round the city

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:09,610
and we'd like to suggest some you may not have thought of.

4
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:12,740
How about a city trip by boat?

5
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:17,509
There are four main stopping points from west to east:

6
00:00:17,509 --> 00:00:26,405
stop A Green Banks, stop B City Bridge, stop C Roman Landing

7
00:00:26,405 --> 00:00:29,310
and stop D Newtown.

8
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:33,960
You can find the main booking office at stop A.

9
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:38,139
The first boat leaves at 8 a.m.

10
00:00:38,139 --> 00:00:40,550
and the last one at 6.30 p.m.

11
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:45,230
There are also many attractions you can visit along the river.

12
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:51,848
At Stop A, if you have time, you can visit the fine 16th century

13
00:00:51,848 --> 00:00:56,420
palace here built for the king with its beautiful formal gardens.

14
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:58,870
It's very near the booking office.

15
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:03,740
Now you can enjoy every corner of this superb residence.

16
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:11,030
Stop B Why don't you visit Tower Restaurant with its wide range of refreshments?

17
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:16,880
This is a place where you can sit and enjoy the wonderful views over the old commercial

18
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:18,750
and banking centre of the city.

19
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:26,818
Stop C is the area where, in the first century AD, invading soldiers crossed

20
00:01:26,818 --> 00:01:27,260
the river;

21
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:30,150
this was much shallower than it is now.

22
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:34,080
That's why this area is called Roman Landing.

23
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:40,170
There's an interactive Museum to visit here with a large shop which has a

24
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:42,140
good range of local history books.

25
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:48,434
At the furthest point of the trip, stop D, the most exciting place to

26
00:01:48,434 --> 00:01:53,986
visit is the new Entertainment Complex with seven-screen cinema, bowling alley

27
00:01:53,986 --> 00:01:55,970
and video games arcade.

28
00:01:55,970 --> 00:02:00,430
Besides the boat tours, there are city buses.

29
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:03,800
Two companies offer special services:

30
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:09,700
The Top Bus Company runs all its tours with a live commentary in English.

31
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:14,607
Tours leave from 8.30 a.m.

32
00:02:14,607 --> 00:02:15,170
every 20 minutes.

33
00:02:15,170 --> 00:02:22,050
There are departures from Central Station, Castle Hill and Long Walk.

34
00:02:22,050 --> 00:02:29,000
This is a hop-on hop-off service and tickets are valid for 24 hours.

35
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:39,080
For further details call Top Bus on 0208 9447810.

36
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:46,630
The Number One Sightseeing Tour is available with a commentary in eight languages.

37
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:53,769
Buses depart from Central Station every five to six minutes from about 9

38
00:02:53,769 --> 00:02:55,132
a.m.

39
00:02:55,132 --> 00:02:58,060
with the last bus at around 7 p.m.

40
00:02:58,060 --> 00:03:03,660
There are also Number One services with an English-speaking...
